# Real fix (2026-08-05): web/Dockerfile's builder stage only ever COPYs
# pipeline/ and web/ (COPY pipeline ./pipeline, COPY web ./web) -- everything
# else at repo root was still being uploaded into the build context on every
# single `docker build .` because there was no .dockerignore at all, with no
# functional purpose (none of it is ever COPY'd into the image). Found the
# hard way while redeploying for #48 slice 6: a stray host-side `cargo build`
# had left root-owned target/ dirs inside pipeline/ and web/ themselves (a
# different, already-understood problem -- BuildKit cache mounts, see this
# Dockerfile's own comment, don't touch a bind-mounted host checkout), and the
# resulting multi-GB build context transfer filled this host's already-tight
# root disk to 100% mid-build (matches this project's own memory note about
# the prior 46GB accumulation incident -- same class of root cause, a
# previously-undiagnosed contributor to it, not a one-off).
.git
.cargo-home
.claude
.claude-flow
.swarm
target
pipeline/target
web/target
runs
test-runs
docs
demo-site
.gitignore
.mcp.json
